Let first be a list of 1 and 3.
Let second be a list of 2.
Let merged be an empty list of whole numbers.
Let i start at 0.
Let j start at 0.
Let first count be count of first.
Let second count be count of second.

Repeat while i < first count and j < second count:
    Let a be item i of first.
    Let b be item j of second.
    If a is at most b:
        Append a to merged.
        Add 1 to i.
    Otherwise:
        Append b to merged.
        Add 1 to j.

Repeat while i < first count:
    Append item i of first to merged.
    Add 1 to i.

Repeat while j < second count:
    Append item j of second to merged.
    Add 1 to j.

Let total be count of merged.
Let middle be total / 2.
Print item middle of merged.
